      </figure>
      <h2 class="newsletter-article-title">ITS for Planned Special Events Executive Briefing &amp; World Cup 2026</h2>
      <div class="newsletter-article-content">
        <p>
          The ITS JPO’s Deployment Evaluation Program (DEP) released five new Executive Briefings on: <a href="https://urldefense.us/v3/__https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fwww.itskrs.its.dot.gov*2Fbriefings*2Fexecutive-briefing*2Fintelligent-transportation-systems-its-planned-special-events-pse/1/0101019f37926a17-134d2286-03c0-4b7e-ba2f-e6acafed2075-000000/fhqNULLHZL_Y7XIcfZkuG8yugAs8Jz-U9q2SFzQBBns=452__;JSUlJSU!!DJ_L93zn18-Ojg!mAIALdMfyE_P1rp1mXIiFy0iNRMhGxytLl31vuD_WCxjec4IAKzfKGRf1pP-WzXAQn1rCAkDcqWIXOXPCcctJt9CtEjU7w$"><em>ITS for Planned Special Events</em></a>, <a href="https://urldefense.us/v3/__https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fwww.itskrs.its.dot.gov*2Fbriefings*2Fexecutive-briefing*2Fintelligent-transportation-systems-asset-management/1/0101019f37926a17-134d2286-03c0-4b7e-ba2f-e6acafed2075-000000/FQB_WfbOwBH763dU73JAt_IVXIVuaFdUQ1Fut8qIRNU=452__;JSUlJSU!!DJ_L93zn18-Ojg!mAIALdMfyE_P1rp1mXIiFy0iNRMhGxytLl31vuD_WCxjec4IAKzfKGRf1pP-WzXAQn1rCAkDcqWIXOXPCcctJt-XqyHocQ$"><em>ITS for Asset Management</em></a>, <a href="https://urldefense.us/v3/__https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fwww.itskrs.its.dot.gov*2Fbriefings*2Fexecutive-briefing*2Fits-cybersecurity-2025-update/1/0101019f37926a17-134d2286-03c0-4b7e-ba2f-e6acafed2075-000000/FDGWdbi9rAz06BtwLzwd0LnZe7Vq92ITI94_2eFvzTA=452__;JSUlJSU!!DJ_L93zn18-Ojg!mAIALdMfyE_P1rp1mXIiFy0iNRMhGxytLl31vuD_WCxjec4IAKzfKGRf1pP-WzXAQn1rCAkDcqWIXOXPCcctJt_gsZRTuQ$"><em>ITS Cybersecurity</em></a>, <a href="https://urldefense.us/v3/__https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fwww.itskrs.its.dot.gov*2Fbriefings*2Fexecutive-briefing*2Fnext-generation-transportation-management-centers-and-transportation/1/0101019f37926a17-134d2286-03c0-4b7e-ba2f-e6acafed2075-000000/TyMabDQuZISfTCltf0t5ll3toBZK-bJZcUPDaHZG9GI=452__;JSUlJSU!!DJ_L93zn18-Ojg!mAIALdMfyE_P1rp1mXIiFy0iNRMhGxytLl31vuD_WCxjec4IAKzfKGRf1pP-WzXAQn1rCAkDcqWIXOXPCcctJt9lhBGRzA$"><em>Next Generation Transportation Management Centers</em></a>, and <a href="https://urldefense.us/v3/__https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fwww.itskrs.its.dot.gov*2Fbriefings*2Fexecutive-briefing*2Ftransit-innovation/1/0101019f37926a17-134d2286-03c0-4b7e-ba2f-e6acafed2075-000000/j0BkDZZx2RKuEIy96tcxuQAs3ibfqrPev9UwW9r1WAM=452__;JSUlJSU!!DJ_L93zn18-Ojg!mAIALdMfyE_P1rp1mXIiFy0iNRMhGxytLl31vuD_WCxjec4IAKzfKGRf1pP-WzXAQn1rCAkDcqWIXOXPCcctJt8pjvYwSA$"><em>Transit Innovation</em></a>.
          These briefings synthesize findings from real-world deployments, highlighting documented benefits, costs, and lessons learned to help transportation agencies make informed investment and operational decisions. As agencies prepare for major events such as large sporting events, festivals, and conventions, the <em>ITS for Planned Special Events</em> briefing offers practical strategies for managing travel demand, reducing congestion, coordinating operations across jurisdictional boundaries, and handling the dramatic, localized travel surges characteristic of major events. The Program looks forward to learning from the innovative transportation strategies, technologies, and operational experiences deployed by host cities during the 2026 FIFA World Cup.
        </p>
        <p>
          Check out the recently released briefings to explore how they help local and regional agencies implement proven technology frameworks that maximize safety and mobility.
        </p>
        <div class="newsletter-cta-wrapper align-right">
