    <article id="world-cup-accessmap" class="newsletter-article">
      <figure class="newsletter-image">
        <img src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/USDOTFHWA/2026/06/13922009/fifa-accessmap_original.png" alt="FIFA AccessMap" />
        <figcaption>Source: SEATTLEFWC26</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2 class="newsletter-article-title">FIFA AccessMap Multimodal Event Edition</h2>
      <div class="newsletter-article-content">
        <p>
          The Taskar Center for Accessible Technology (TCAT) at the University of Washington (UW) partnered with the Seattle FIFA World Cup 2026 Local Organizing Committee to develop custom AccessMap features. TCAT is one of the primary awardees selected to lead a major deployment site under the ITS JPO’s ITS4US Deployment Program, a multimodal initiative that improves transportation efficiency while creating strong public-private partnerships, implementing innovative solutions, and delivering cost-saving results that other communities can scale and replicate.
        </p>
        <p>
          The result is the FIFA AccessMap Multimodal Event Edition, which delivers an accessibility-first, multimodal trip planning experience. This tool is integrated directly into the official FIFA local apps (SEA &amp; WIN) for the Puget Sound region. AccessMap now appears alongside Google Maps and Apple Maps as a first-class navigation option, representing a genuine, high-visibility real-world deployment of UW’s Transportation Data Exchange approach-more than just a standalone demonstration.
        </p>
        <div class="newsletter-cta-wrapper align-right">
          <a href="https://urldefense.us/v3/__https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fwww.seattlefwc26.org*2Fdestination*2Ftransportation/1/0101019f37926a17-134d2286-03c0-4b7e-ba2f-e6acafed2075-000000/9tHWhm5VyUquPUXRPb4RtCgCYQPsuSSL8GGREy3m-Eo=452__;JSUlJQ!!DJ_L93zn18-Ojg!mAIALdMfyE_P1rp1mXIiFy0iNRMhGxytLl31vuD_WCxjec4IAKzfKGRf1pP-WzXAQn1rCAkDcqWIXOXPCcctJt_dsvGKVA$" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="newsletter-cta"><strong>AccessMap at FIFA 2026</strong></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article id="its4us-deployment-accelerator-program" class="newsletter-article">
      <figure class="newsletter-image">
        <img src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/USDOTFHWA/2026/06/13922011/its4us-accelerator-logo_original.png" alt="ITS4US Accelerator" />
        <figcaption>Source: USDOT</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2 class="newsletter-article-title">ITS4US Deployment Accelerator Program: Bringing American Innovation to Your Community</h2>
      <div class="newsletter-article-content">
        <p>
          The ITS4US Deployment Accelerator Program is a new ITS JPO initiative, in coordination with the Federal Transit Administration. This program aims to significantly accelerate targeted follow-on deployments by rapidly replicating the open-source code developed by the Heart of Iowa Regional Transit Agency (HIRTA) ITS4US deployment site. This solicitation, expected to be released in late 2026, will award multiple sites with seed funding to assess the replicability of HIRTA’s solution in various operating environments.
        </p>
        <div class="newsletter-cta-wrapper align-right">
          <a href="https://urldefense.us/v3/__https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fits.dot.gov*2Fresearch-areas*2FITS4US*2Fupcoming*2F/1/0101019f37926a17-134d2286-03c0-4b7e-ba2f-e6acafed2075-000000/Vj0Zp8j-oDCNn4tLs2WmuftzUp5IPYt-TOiOcqXMtPw=452__;JSUlJSUl!!DJ_L93zn18-Ojg!mAIALdMfyE_P1rp1mXIiFy0iNRMhGxytLl31vuD_WCxjec4IAKzfKGRf1pP-WzXAQn1rCAkDcqWIXOXPCcctJt_pnuBv1w$" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="newsletter-cta"><strong>ITS4US Deployment Accelerator Program Info</strong></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

