    <article id="missed-the-ai-innovation-exchange-webinars-recordings-available" class="newsletter-article">
      <figure class="newsletter-image">
        <img src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/USDOTFHWA/2026/06/13922029/6972928/ai-and-data-webinar_crop.png" alt="AI and Data Webinar" />
        <figcaption>Source: FHWA</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2 class="newsletter-article-title">Missed the AI Innovation Exchange Webinars? Recordings Available!</h2>
      <div class="newsletter-article-content">
        <p>
          The ITS JPO AI Program kicked off the FHWA Center for Local Aid Support (CLAS) Innovation Exchange Webinar on May 21, 2026. The webinar titled, “AI in Transportation: Data Collection for Asset Management,” featured a presentation on “AI and Data Strategic Considerations,” focusing on data governance, collection, management, integration and critical considerations around quality, privacy, security for implementing AI in transportation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Subsequently, the ITS JPO AI Program hosted another FHWA CLAS Innovation Exchange Webinar on June 25, 2026. The webinar titled “AI in Transportation: Project Delivery” featured a presentation on how AI can support specific needs and phases during transportation project delivery. The presentation shared example AI uses cases and applications for environmental, design, right of way and utility coordination, project procurement, project close out, and project operations and maintenance.
        </p>
        <div class="newsletter-cta-wrapper align-right">
