    <article id="two-new-its-short-course-instructor-kits-now-available" class="newsletter-article">
      <figure class="newsletter-image">
        <img src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/USDOTFHWA/2026/06/13922030/6972930/its-short-courses-july-jpo-now_crop.png" alt="ITS Short Courses" />
        <figcaption>Source: iStock/chombosan (left) /iStock/NicoElNino (right)</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2 class="newsletter-article-title">Two New ITS Short Course Instructor Kits Now Available!</h2>
      <div class="newsletter-article-content">
        <p>
          The ITS JPO released two free instructor kits that can be used to teach the basics of ITS to students and early career professionals. Each kit includes a slide deck, participant workbook, hands-on activities, and instructor notes. No development time required. Just download, teach, and inspire the next generation of transportation innovators. These ready-to-use modules were developed with input from transportation practitioners and are designed to be easily incorporated into your course curriculum, training programs, and/or onboarding activities.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Introduction to Intelligent Transportation Systems</strong> – A 90-minute module covering real-world ITS deployments, transportation challenges, and career pathways. Search for Course #137000.</li>
          <li><strong>Applying Systems Engineering to ITS Projects</strong> – A 90-minute module walking trainees through the Vee model, ConOps development, and stakeholder coordination. Search for Course #137999.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="newsletter-cta-wrapper align-right">
          <a href="https://urldefense.us/v3/__https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Ffhwanhi.geniussis.com*2FRegistrationByCourse.aspx/2/0101019f37926a17-134d2286-03c0-4b7e-ba2f-e6acafed2075-000000/5vGWkZiT9dw3qC8dRCnBo5KH0Dvu796pW6K7Iam27jw=452__;JSUl!!DJ_L93zn18-Ojg!mAIALdMfyE_P1rp1mXIiFy0iNRMhGxytLl31vuD_WCxjec4IAKzfKGRf1pP-WzXAQn1rCAkDcqWIXOXPCcctJt-3xeVaZQ$" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="newsletter-cta"><strong>Access the Instructor Kits</strong></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article id="arizona-texas-utah-v2x-accelerator-sites-featured" class="newsletter-article">
      <figure class="newsletter-image">
        <img src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/USDOTFHWA/2026/06/13922031/6972931/jponews-v2x-its-international_crop.png" alt="JPO News V2X International" />
        <figcaption>Source: ITS International</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2 class="newsletter-article-title">Arizona, Texas, and Utah V2X Accelerator Sites Featured in ITS International</h2>
      <div class="newsletter-article-content">
        <p>
          The Texas A&amp;M Transportation Institute (TTI) and Utah DOT (UDOT) V2X Accelerator deployments were recently featured in the March/April 2026 edition of ITS International while the Maricopa County DOT (MCDOT) V2X Accelerator deployment was featured in the May/June 2026 edition. The articles discuss how MCDOT, TTI, and UDOT demonstrate how V2X can save lives today while paving the way for a safer, more connected transportation future and include quotes from representatives from each of the three sites.
        </p>
        <div class="newsletter-cta-wrapper align-right">
          <a href="https://urldefense.us/v3/__https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fdigital.itsinternational.com*2F2026*2Fmay-jun*2Fhtml5*2F/1/0101019f37926a17-134d2286-03c0-4b7e-ba2f-e6acafed2075-000000/9clIfFfEI2YP-_0gHyBrbozeLRbaUwdmuXRpRg8X9iM=452__;JSUlJSUl!!DJ_L93zn18-Ojg!mAIALdMfyE_P1rp1mXIiFy0iNRMhGxytLl31vuD_WCxjec4IAKzfKGRf1pP-WzXAQn1rCAkDcqWIXOXPCcctJt9KwpLA4A$" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="newsletter-cta"><strong>Read the MCDOT Article</strong></a>
        </div>
        <div class="newsletter-cta-wrapper align-right">
          <a href="https://urldefense.us/v3/__https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fdigital.itsinternational.com*2F2026*2Fmar-apr*2Fhtml5*2F/1/0101019f37926a17-134d2286-03c0-4b7e-ba2f-e6acafed2075-000000/C74YEY99Of9Mcf4U7-mkxOs3acKFYevKcALpulaoI48=452__;JSUlJSUl!!DJ_L93zn18-Ojg!mAIALdMfyE_P1rp1mXIiFy0iNRMhGxytLl31vuD_WCxjec4IAKzfKGRf1pP-WzXAQn1rCAkDcqWIXOXPCcctJt_FCzFM3w$" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="newsletter-cta"><strong>Read the TTI and UDOT Articles</strong></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article id="tti-v2x-accelerator-site-hosts-usdot-for-visit" class="newsletter-article">
      <figure class="newsletter-image">
        <img src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/USDOTFHWA/2026/06/13922033/jponews-v2x-tti_original.png" alt="JPO News TTI" />
        <figcaption>Source: TTI</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2 class="newsletter-article-title">TTI V2X Accelerator Site Hosts USDOT for Visit</h2>
      <div class="newsletter-article-content">
        <p>
          TTI hosted USDOT on May 18-21 for an operational readiness check. During the visit, TTI walked through their 15 V2X use cases and demonstrated their current operational functionality at their RELLIS campus test track and within deployment sites throughout College Station and Houston. The TTI team demonstrated the use of both direct and network V2X use cases using roadside units deployed at real-intersections within Houston and the SH6-US290 corridor and onboard units instrumented in several test vehicles. The readiness check validated these operational use cases in a real-world environment and helped identify lessons learned that will help inform future V2X implementations.
        </p>
        <div class="newsletter-cta-wrapper align-right">
          <a href="https://urldefense.us/v3/__https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fwww.its.dot.gov*2Fresearch-areas*2FV2X-Deployment*2Fdeployment*2Faccelerator*2Ftexas-am*2F/1/0101019f37926a17-134d2286-03c0-4b7e-ba2f-e6acafed2075-000000/lI5ibu5Bb8M-n8rl4cIt7CQLgpMOsEZ2KgeBCs1tTIA=452__;JSUlJSUlJSU!!DJ_L93zn18-Ojg!mAIALdMfyE_P1rp1mXIiFy0iNRMhGxytLl31vuD_WCxjec4IAKzfKGRf1pP-WzXAQn1rCAkDcqWIXOXPCcctJt8k2EfiAg$" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="newsletter-cta"><strong>Additional TTI V2X Accelerator Site Info</strong></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article id="its-retrospective-analysis-report-now-available" class="newsletter-article">
      <figure class="newsletter-image">
        <img src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/USDOTFHWA/2026/06/13938341/publication-its-retrospective-analysis-and-looking-_original.png" alt="Retrospective Analysis and Looking Into the Future Report" />
        <figcaption>Source: Getty Images/ Choi Dongsu</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2 class="newsletter-article-title">ITS Retrospective Analysis and Looking Into the Future Report Now Available!</h2>
      <div class="newsletter-article-content">
        <p>
          The ITS JPO recently released the Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITS) Retrospective Analysis and Looking Into the Future Report, which provides a comprehensive overview of the history, current state, and future outlook for ITS in improving safety, mobility, and efficiency across all modes of transportation. The Report aims to capture key milestones achieved in the ITS industry, investments, priorities, transformative technologies, and opportunities to accelerate ITS while also highlighting the importance of collaboration between public and private sectors, new procurement models, and opportunities to accelerate the advancement of ITS in the transportation industry. View full report via the button below!
        </p>
        <div class="newsletter-cta-wrapper align-right">
          <a href="https://urldefense.us/v3/__https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Frosap.ntl.bts.gov*2Fview*2Fdot*2F92128/1/0101019f37926a17-134d2286-03c0-4b7e-ba2f-e6acafed2075-000000/M24J7-fMB6ODvOm8vthtV4-UmsIeKgJqrf9KtR5Zv7I=452__;JSUlJSU!!DJ_L93zn18-Ojg!mAIALdMfyE_P1rp1mXIiFy0iNRMhGxytLl31vuD_WCxjec4IAKzfKGRf1pP-WzXAQn1rCAkDcqWIXOXPCcctJt9d-aRWCQ$" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="newsletter-cta"><strong>ITS Retrospective Analysis and Looking Into the Future Full Report</strong></a>
        </div>
